    tick_increment: TickIncrementRawPair;
    market_flow_indicator: bytes &size=2;
    group_instrument: bytes &size=2;
    instrument: bytes &size=4;
    instrument_external_code: bytes &size=30;
    contract_size: bytes &size=8;
    # Tick Value Fraction Pair is the same bytes whichever arm the model names: its arms lay them out alike and differ only in what they are called and what they mean, which Tick Value Fraction Indicator says (Tick Value Negative Whole Pair, Tick Value Negative Ten Pair, Tick Value Negative Hundred Pair, Tick Value Negative Thousand Pair, Tick Value Negative Ten Thousand Pair, Tick Value Negative Hundred Thousand Pair, Tick Value Negative Million Pair, Tick Value Numeric Pair). They are parsed as TickValueNumericPair, so which arm applies is left to what is built on the definition.
